SEND(2)                        P32W Unix                         SEND(2)

NAME
       send, recv, sendto, recvfrom, shutdown - data on sockets

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/socket.h>

       ssize_t send(int fd, const void *buf, size_t n, int flags);
       ssize_t recv(int fd, void *buf, size_t n, int flags);
       ssize_t sendto(int fd, const void *buf, size_t n, int flags,
                      const struct sockaddr *to, socklen_t tolen);
       ssize_t recvfrom(int fd, void *buf, size_t n, int flags,
                        struct sockaddr *from, socklen_t *fromlen);
       int shutdown(int fd, int how);

DESCRIPTION
       On a stream socket, send is write(2) and recv is read(2),
       with flags: write sends all n bytes, waiting for room as it
       goes; read returns what has arrived (up to n, and at most
       1024 at a time), waits if nothing has, and returns 0 at the
       end of the stream, when the peer has shut down its side.

       On a datagram socket each send is one datagram (1018 bytes
       at most), to the address given to sendto or, for send and
       write, to connect(2)'s. Each recv takes one datagram;
       recvfrom also gives the sender's address. A datagram socket
       not yet used gets a port when it first sends.

       MSG_DONTWAIT in flags makes this one call fail with EAGAIN
       rather than wait, as O_NONBLOCK does for every call.

       shutdown(fd, SHUT_WR) or SHUT_RDWR ends the sending side of
       a stream: the peer reads the end of the stream, and this
       side can still read the answer. SHUT_RD does nothing.

RETURN VALUE
       The bytes sent or received; shutdown 0. -1 on an error, with
       errno set.

ERRORS
       EAGAIN          Nothing to read, or no room to send, and not
                       waiting.
       EPIPE           The connection is gone: SIGPIPE is sent too,
                       as for a pipe.
       ECONNRESET      The peer reset the connection.
       ENOTCONN        Not connected.
       EDESTADDRREQ    A datagram with no address to go to.
       EMSGSIZE        A datagram too long.
       EOPNOTSUPP      MSG_PEEK.
       EINTR           A signal came while waiting.

SEE ALSO
       socket(2), read(2), write(2), select(2)

BUGS
       No MSG_PEEK or out-of-band data.
